{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwMul","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwGram"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.two_mul_trace_lmul_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.two_mul_trace_lmul_σ","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L126-L135","doc":"**The trace of a generator, in closed form.**  Stated doubled so no\ndivision is needed and the statement holds in any characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.two_mul_card_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.two_mul_card_descent","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L111-L124","doc":"**Exactly half the permutations have a descent at `i`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.card_descent_eq_card_ascent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.card_descent_eq_card_ascent","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L91-L109","doc":"Right multiplication by `s_i` swaps ascents and descents at `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.trace_lmul_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.trace_lmul_σ","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**The trace of a generator is counted by descents.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.repr_σ_mul_Tw_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.repr_σ_mul_Tw_diag","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L61-L78","doc":"**Only descents contribute.**  The diagonal coefficient of `σ_i · T_w` is\n`0` when the length goes up and `q - 1` when it goes down — the `q`-term of\nthe down case lands on `T_{w s_i}`, off the diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.trace_lmul_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.trace_lmul_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L50-L59","doc":"**The regular trace is the sum of the diagonal coefficients** of left\nmultiplication, read in the `T_w` basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.repr_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.repr_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwTrace.lean#L45-L48","doc":"The basis coordinates of a basis vector: `⟨T_v⟩_w = δ_{v,w}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}